msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:21465
msgid "Likely interview themes"
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:21466
msgid "interview questions template"
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:21473
msgid "What to expect from this process"
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:21474
msgid "hiring guide template"
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:21973
#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22126
msgid "the market"
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:21983
#, php-format
msgid "The role was posted %s, so fast follow-up matters."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:21984
msgid "Treat the role as live and move quickly after applying."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:21986
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Use the extra context you shared (%s) to sharpen the proof points you lead "
"with."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:21987
msgid ""
"Lead with the most relevant proof of fit before asking for more of the "
"recruiter’s time."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:21995
#, php-format
msgid "Lead with role fit, not a cold request, for %s at %s."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:21996
#, php-format
msgid ""
"This role sits in %s and is tied to %s, so the strongest outreach is short, "
"specific, and anchored to one or two signals from the brief rather than a "
"broad networking ask. %s"
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:21997
#, php-format
msgid ""
"The brief appears to prioritise %s and %s, so your first message should "
"sound informed rather than exploratory."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22002
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Approach %s as the route into the process, not as someone you need to "
"impress with a long story."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22003
msgid ""
"Treat the recruiter touchpoint as a way to signal fit and timing, then move "
"quickly into a role-specific conversation."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22004
#, php-format
msgid ""
"For a %s role in %s, recruiters usually respond better to concise evidence "
"of fit, location alignment, and timing than to generic enthusiasm."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22007
#, php-format
msgid "One direct line on your fit for %s."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22008
#, php-format
msgid "Evidence that you already understand the %s angle of the mandate."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22009
#, php-format
msgid "A short proof point linked to %s."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22010
#, php-format
msgid "A reason your background fits %s or the wider %s market."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22013
msgid "Do not open by asking for a referral in the first line."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22014
msgid ""
"Do not send a generic “would love to connect” note with no role context."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22015
msgid "Do not describe your whole CV when one sharp proof point will do."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22020
msgid ""
"Use the recruiter touchpoint first, then move toward the most relevant team-"
"side contact once you have established fit and timing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22021
msgid ""
"Earn a reply or short exchange first, then ask whether there is someone "
"closer to the team you should speak with before making a referral request."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22022
msgid ""
"Ask only after you have established a credible role fit, shown you "
"understand the brief, and either applied already or are ready to apply "
"immediately."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22024
#, php-format
msgid "You can clearly explain why %s is the right next step."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22025
#, php-format
msgid "You have one or two relevant proof points tied to %s."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22026
msgid "Your request feels timely rather than speculative."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22029
msgid "Do not ask strangers to “refer me” before earning any engagement."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22030
msgid "Do not overstate closeness or shared connection if it is weak."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22038
msgid ""
"Start here if you need process clarity, timing signals, or a direct route "
"into the role."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22041
#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22105
#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22247
#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:35516
msgid "Relevant team-side contact"
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22042
#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22106
#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22314
#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22362
msgid "Team-side perspective"
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22043
msgid ""
"Useful for insider context on the mandate, team rhythm, and what strong "
"candidates usually demonstrate."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22048
msgid "Alumni or warm second-degree connection"
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22049
#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22369
msgid "Warm introduction route"
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22050
msgid ""
"Best used once you can show role-specific knowledge and a credible reason to "
"be introduced."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22053
msgid ""
"Start with the most relevant recruiter or current team-side contact, build "
"signal first, then use any warmer connection for momentum rather than as "
"your first move."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22057
msgid "Apply or prepare to apply"
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22058
msgid "Immediately"
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22059
msgid ""
"Get your application state ready so your outreach can mention that you have "
"applied or are submitting now."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22060
msgid "Show momentum and seriousness."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22063
msgid "Send a short recruiter note"
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22064
msgid "Within 24 hours"
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22065
msgid ""
"Lead with fit, one signal from the brief, and why this role at this firm is "
"relevant for you."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22066
msgid "Earn a reply or recognition in the process."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22069
msgid "Follow up once"
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22070
msgid "3 to 4 days later"
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22071
msgid ""
"Add one sharper proof point or update rather than repeating the first note."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22072
msgid "Move from cold outreach to an informed conversation."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22076
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Hi %1$s, I’m reaching out about the %2$s role at %3$s because the brief’s "
"focus on %4$s lines up closely with my background in %5$s. I wanted to start "
"with one short, role-specific question rather than send a broad networking "
"note. If there is one signal strong candidates usually show early, I would "
"value your steer."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22077
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Strategy: Keep the note short, lead with one signal from the role, and make "
"the ask feel light.\\n\\nInMail: Hi %1$s, I’m interested in the %2$s role at "
"%3$s. My background lines up with %4$s, and the brief’s focus on %5$s stood "
"out. I wanted to introduce myself with a short role-specific note and ask "
"what strong candidates tend to signal early in process."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22078
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Email:\\nSubject: %1$s role at %2$s\\n\\nHi %3$s,\\n\\nI’m writing regarding "
"the %1$s opportunity at %2$s. The brief’s emphasis on %4$s caught my "
"attention, and I felt my background in %5$s was relevant enough to reach out "
"directly. I would value any guidance on what the team tends to prioritise in "
"strong candidates for this mandate.\\n\\nBest,\\n%6$s\\n\\nReferral ask:"
"\\nThanks again for the exchange on the %1$s role. I wanted to ask whether "
"there is someone closer to the %2$s team or process who it would make sense "
"for me to speak with, given my background in %5$s and interest in this "
"mandate."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22081
msgid ""
"Start with a short insight-led note that proves you understand the brief "
"before you ask for time, access, or a referral."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22083
#, php-format
msgid "Reference one concrete signal from the brief such as %s."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22084
#, php-format
msgid "Show how your background connects to %s."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22085
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Explain why %s at %s is relevant rather than speaking broadly about private "
"equity roles."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22088
msgid "Generic “would love to connect” messages with no role context."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22089
msgid "Asking for a referral before establishing fit or timing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22090
msgid "Requesting too much time before earning any engagement."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22092
msgid ""
"Follow up once after a few days with one sharper signal or update. If there "
"is still no response, move to a better-matched contact instead of repeating "
"the same ask."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22097
msgid ""
"Best for timing clarity, process context, and getting on the radar without "
"overcomplicating the ask."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22099
#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22307
msgid "5 min telephone call"
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22100
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Lead with one role-specific fit point tied to %s and why this mandate at %s "
"stands out."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22101
msgid "Avoid asking for a referral or coffee chat in the first line."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22102
msgid "Best used once your application is ready or already submitted."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22107
msgid ""
"Best for understanding what strong candidates usually sound like and what "
"context matters internally."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22108
#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22318
msgid "LinkedIn DM"
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22109
#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22319
msgid "Coffee meeting"
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22110
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Lead with curiosity about how %s shows up in the actual work, not with a "
"direct request for access."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22111
msgid "Avoid making it sound like a hidden referral request."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22112
msgid ""
"Best used before or shortly after applying, while the role still feels "
"current."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22117
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Strategy: Ask for a very short call only after showing clear role context. "
"Keep the ask narrow and make it easy to decline.\\n\\nMessage: Hi [Name], "
"I’m reaching out regarding the %1$s role at %2$s. I have one specific "
"question about how the team values %3$s and would be grateful for a quick 5 "
"minute call if easier than email."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22148
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Use the extra context you added (%s) as supporting proof, not as the opening "
"line."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22149
msgid "Lead with one sharp proof point rather than a long background summary."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22152
#, php-format
msgid ""
"For %1$s at %2$s, the best first move is to lead with %3$s before you ask "
"for access."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22153
#, php-format
msgid ""
"The sharper route into %1$s at %2$s is to prove %3$s, then ask a focused "
"question."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22154
#, php-format
msgid ""
"A stronger opening for %1$s is to show you already understand %2$s, not just "
"that you want the role."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22155
#, php-format
msgid ""
"This %1$s role rewards context-first outreach: show %2$s, then move toward "
"conversation."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22159
#, php-format
msgid ""
"This role sits in %1$s and appears to care about %2$s and %3$s. That means "
"the best networking move is not a generic request for time, but a short note "
"that sounds like you already understand the brief, the team shape, and the "
"hiring signal in %4$s. %5$s"
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22160
#, php-format
msgid ""
"MENA Careers would not open this with a broad “would love to connect” note. "
"For %1$s at %2$s, a better path is to anchor your outreach to %3$s, connect "
"it to %4$s, and make the first ask small enough to earn a reply. %5$s"
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22161
#, php-format
msgid ""
"The live brief points toward %1$s rather than generic enthusiasm. In "
"practice that means your outreach should sound like someone already tracking "
"%2$s in %3$s, not someone asking strangers to explain the whole process. %4$s"
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22162
#, php-format
msgid ""
"The networking angle here is narrower and more tactical than most job "
"seekers assume. For %1$s, your message needs to carry proof around %2$s, "
"timing discipline, and a credible reason to be speaking to this team in %3$s "
"right now. %4$s"
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22166
#, php-format
msgid ""
"The brief leans toward %1$s and %2$s, so outreach should reference those "
"signals before anything personal."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22167
#, php-format
msgid ""
"What stands out most is the combination of %1$s with %2$s. That is a better "
"opening signal than generic interest in %3$s."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22168
#, php-format
msgid ""
"The role appears to reward candidates who can speak to %1$s in a %2$s "
"context."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22169
#, php-format
msgid ""
"A smarter first note would sound informed about %1$s and %2$s rather than "
"broad ambitions."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22174
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Because the role appears newly live (%s), speed matters. A concise, role-"
"aware message is better than a polished but delayed one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22174
msgid "recently posted"
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22175
msgid ""
"This looks like a fresh opportunity, so a fast, context-rich first touch is "
"more valuable than waiting to craft a perfect note."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22178
#, php-format
msgid ""
"The role is still active (%s), so the best move is to reach out while the "
"mandate feels current and the recruiter can still place your name quickly."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22178
msgid "currently live"
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22179
msgid ""
"The timing window is still open, which makes a short role-specific message "
"more useful than a long networking build-up."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22182
#, php-format
msgid ""
"The posting timing (%s) suggests you need more context in the first note to "
"avoid sounding late or generic."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22182
msgid "live for a while"
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22183
msgid ""
"This does not look like a brand-new posting, so the first message should "
"carry more context and a clearer reason to respond now."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22188
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Open on %1$s, then make a small ask around %2$s rather than asking "
"immediately for a meeting or referral."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22189
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Treat the first note as a calibration message: prove %1$s, show awareness of "
"%2$s, and only then ask for a short steer."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22190
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Use %1$s as the anchor and frame your message around why this specific %2$s "
"role at %3$s is the right fit."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22191
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Lead with one crisp fit point tied to %1$s. The best outcome of the first "
"touch is not a long conversation, but a credible reply."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22195
#, php-format
msgid ""
"For a %1$s role in %2$s, the recruiter is more likely to respond to clear "
"signals of fit than to broad networking intent."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22196
#, php-format
msgid ""
"This works because %1$s is easier to validate quickly than a long story "
"about motivation, especially when the brief already signals %2$s."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22197
#, php-format
msgid ""
"A short, informed opening reduces the risk of being grouped with low-context "
"outreach, which is common for %1$s roles."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22198
#, php-format
msgid ""
"The first message needs to sound like it belongs in the process already. "
"Referencing %1$s helps do that quickly."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22202
#, php-format
msgid "A direct proof point showing exposure to %s."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22203
#, php-format
msgid "One credible sentence linking your background to %s."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22204
#, php-format
msgid "A role-specific reason %s at %s is relevant for you now."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22205
#, php-format
msgid "If true, a location or language signal that supports working in %s."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22209
msgid "Do not ask for a referral in the first line."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22210
msgid ""
"Do not send a generic “would love to connect” request with no role context."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22211
msgid "Do not paste your whole background when one strong proof point will do."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22212
msgid "Do not make the first ask bigger than the context you have earned."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22216
msgid ""
"Start with the recruiter route for timing and process clarity, then move "
"toward the most relevant team-side contact once you can sound informed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22217
msgid ""
"Use the recruiter touchpoint to get into the process, then use a team-side "
"contact to sharpen context rather than to force a referral."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22218
msgid ""
"The strongest path is a two-step route: signal fit through the recruiter, "
"then deepen credibility with the most relevant team-side voice."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22220
msgid ""
"Without a clear team-side route, earn a short exchange first and only then "
"ask whether there is someone closer to the mandate you should learn from."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22221
msgid ""
"Treat the recruiter route as primary until you have enough context to "
"justify being redirected closer to the team."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22222
msgid ""
"The cleanest route here is to sound process-aware first, then ask whether "
"there is a better person to speak with about the mandate."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22226
msgid ""
"Ask only after you have shown role-specific interest and earned at least one "
"useful exchange; junior private equity candidates are penalized quickly for "
"asking too early."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22227
msgid ""
"Do not ask in the first interaction. Ask after you have demonstrated fit and "
"have something concrete to be referred for."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22229
msgid ""
"Ask once your fit is clear, your application state is ready, and the person "
"you are messaging has enough context to attach your name to the role."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22230
msgid ""
"Ask after you have created some context and can point to a specific reason "
"you would be credible in process, not before."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22234
#, php-format
msgid "You can explain why %s is the right next step for you."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22235
#, php-format
msgid "You can point to a specific fit signal around %s."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22236
msgid "Your application timing feels real rather than speculative."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22237
msgid "Your ask is small enough to be reasonable for a first exchange."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22241
msgid ""
"Do not turn an insight conversation into a referral request too quickly."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22242
msgid ""
"Do not ask multiple people at the same firm for the same favour at once."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22243
msgid "Do not request access if you cannot yet explain your fit clearly."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22249
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Start with %1$s or the process-facing route, then move to %2$s once you can "
"ask sharper questions."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22250
#, php-format
msgid ""
"The best sequence is process first, context second: use %1$s for timing, "
"then %2$s for insight."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22251
msgid ""
"Use your first touch to get into the right lane, then speak to someone "
"closer to the work once you can sound informed rather than curious from "
"scratch."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22255
msgid ""
"Get your application ready first so your first message can say you have "
"already applied or are about to submit."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22256
msgid ""
"Prepare one short outreach message tied to the brief before asking for time."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22258
msgid ""
"After the first touch, move to a team-side contact with one focused question "
"that proves you read the role properly."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22259
msgid ""
"Follow up with one sharper signal or update instead of repeating the "
"original outreach."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22261
#, php-format
msgid "Align your follow-up with the likely process signal: %s."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22262
msgid ""
"Only escalate the ask once you have either a reply, a warm hint, or clear "
"proof of fit to reference."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22265
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Lead with one tight line on %1$s, then ask a small question that makes sense "
"for a %2$s role at %3$s."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22266
#, php-format
msgid ""
"The best opening move is not a meeting request. It is a short role-aware "
"note that proves you understand %1$s and why it matters here."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22267
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Open with context, not ambition. Show %1$s first, then ask for the smallest "
"useful steer."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22268
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Make the first note easy to answer: one proof point, one specific signal "
"about %1$s, and one small ask."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22272
#, php-format
msgid "Reference one visible signal from the brief such as %s."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22273
#, php-format
msgid "Connect your background to %s rather than to “finance” broadly."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22274
#, php-format
msgid "Explain why %s in %s is relevant for you now."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22277
#, php-format
msgid "If true, mention your exposure to %s as supporting context."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22281
msgid "Messages that ask for time before showing any role-specific context."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22282
msgid ""
"Opening with broad interest in finance or investing without a private "
"equity, market-specific, or role-specific angle."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22283
msgid "Reaching out in the wrong tone for the role’s seniority or timing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22286
msgid ""
"Writing a long LinkedIn message when a tighter note would be easier to "
"answer."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22288
msgid ""
"Sending a polished but generic email that could have been sent to any firm."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22290
msgid ""
"Applying silently and only networking later, after the context window has "
"faded."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22294
msgid ""
"Follow up once after a few days with one sharper signal, update, or "
"question. Do not resend the same message."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22295
msgid ""
"One follow-up is enough. If there is still no reply, improve the angle or "
"move to a better-matched contact."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22296
msgid ""
"Use the follow-up to add context, not pressure. A better signal is stronger "
"than a second generic request."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22304
msgid ""
"Best for timing clarity, recruiter process signals, and getting your name "
"onto the right lane quickly."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22305
msgid ""
"Best for knowing whether the role is moving now, what matters first, and how "
"to position your first touch."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22307
msgid "Insight request"
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22308
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Lead with %1$s and one direct reason this %2$s role is relevant for you now."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22309
msgid "Avoid treating the first note like a favour request or a coffee ask."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22310
msgid "Best used immediately while the role still feels newly live."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22310
msgid ""
"Best used once you can point to a ready application or clear fit signal."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22316
msgid ""
"Best for understanding what the mandate actually sounds like internally and "
"how candidates usually stand out."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22317
msgid ""
"Best used as the type of person you should look for next, once the process-"
"facing route has given you enough context."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22319
msgid "Zoom call"
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22320
#, php-format
msgid "Lead with one focused question on how %s shows up in the actual work."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22321
msgid "Avoid turning the first exchange into an obvious referral ask."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22322
msgid ""
"Best used after you have a better sense of the mandate and can ask more "
"intelligent questions."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22327
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Hi [Name], I’m looking closely at the %1$s role at %2$s and wanted to avoid "
"sending a generic message. The brief’s focus on %3$s is especially relevant "
"to my background, and I wondered if you might be open to a short coffee so I "
"can ask one or two more informed questions about the team and the role."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22328
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Hi [Name], I’m preparing a thoughtful application for the %1$s role at %2$s "
"and was struck by the emphasis on %3$s. If useful, I’d value a short Zoom "
"call to ask a couple of focused questions so my application reflects the "
"role more accurately."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22329
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Hi [Name], I’m reaching out about the %1$s opportunity at %2$s. I have one "
"short question around how the team thinks about %3$s and would be grateful "
"for a brief 5 minute call if easier than email."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22330
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Hi [Name], I’m interested in the %1$s role at %2$s and wanted to reach out "
"in a role-specific way rather than a generic one. If you are ever open to a "
"brief in-person catch up, I’d appreciate the chance to ask a few focused "
"questions about the mandate and how candidates stand out."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22358
msgid "Start here if you need timing, clarity, or a process-aware first touch."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22363
msgid ""
"Use next when you want sharper context on how the mandate is actually "
"discussed internally."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22368
msgid "Warm second-degree connection"
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22370
msgid ""
"Best used after you have already built enough context to justify an "
"introduction."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22377
msgid "Position your first note"
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22380
msgid "Make the first touch feel timely and specific."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22383
msgid "Earn a reply, not a favour"
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22384
msgid "After the first touch"
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22386
msgid "Move from cold outreach into a more credible exchange."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22389
msgid "Escalate only with context"
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22390
msgid "If you receive a response or signal"
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22392
msgid "Keep the outreach disciplined and role-aware."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22396
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Hi %1$s, I’m reaching out about the %2$s role at %3$s because the brief’s "
"emphasis on %4$s stood out and feels especially relevant to my background. I "
"wanted to ask one short role-specific question rather than send a broad "
"networking note, as you seemed like the most relevant person to approach "
"first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22397
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Strategy: Use LinkedIn when the role is current, keep the note under 5 "
"lines, and lead with one credible proof point.\\n\\nInMail: Hi %1$s, I’m "
"reaching out about the %2$s role at %3$s. My background has made %4$s "
"particularly relevant, and I was struck by the role’s focus on %5$s. I’d "
"value any steer on what strong candidates typically signal early in process."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22398
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Email:\\nSubject: %1$s role at %2$s\\n\\nHi %3$s,\\n\\nI’m writing regarding "
"the %1$s opportunity at %2$s. The brief’s focus on %4$s is especially "
"relevant to my background, and I wanted to introduce myself with a short "
"role-specific note rather than a broad networking email. If useful, I’d "
"value any guidance on what the team tends to prioritise early in process."
"\\n\\nBest,\\n%5$s\\n\\nReferral ask:\\nThanks again for the earlier steer "
"on the %1$s role. Based on our exchange around %4$s, I wanted to ask whether "
"there is someone closer to the mandate who it would make sense for me to "
"speak with before I take the next step in process."
msgstr ""

#: includes/crm/class-crm-shortcodes.php:22408
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Strategy: Ask for a quick call only after proving role fit and keep the ask "
"specific.\\n\\nMessage: Hi [Name], I’m reaching out regarding the %1$s role "
"at %2$s. I have one focused question about how the team values %3$s and "
"would be grateful for a quick 5 minute call if easier than email."
msgstr ""

